---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SetupPrompt from "~app/guide/components/SetupPrompt";

const title = "Join Shoal — direct fork setup";
const description =
  "Directly fork the Shoal Network Root, complete Actions onboarding, and set up your Reviewer Node with a personal Review Policy.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="wrap guide-page">
    <p class="section-kicker">BECOME A REVIEWER</p>
    <h1>Join Shoal</h1>
    <p>
      The direct fork is the join action. There is no website account or
      approval form. Directory appearance follows current eligibility and the
      next successful full projection publication.
    </p>
    <h2>Manual setup</h2>
    <ol class="onboarding-steps">
      <li>
        <strong>
          Directly fork the canonical{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/taco3064/shoal-station/fork">
            Network Root ↗
          </a>
        </strong>{" "}
        into your personal GitHub account. Forking another Reviewer Node does
        not qualify.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open your new fork’s GitHub Actions page</strong> and personally
        complete GitHub’s manual enable / confirmation before running init.
        Repository-level Actions permissions and a workflow shown as active do
        not prove this historical UI step occurred.
      </li>
      <li>
        Clone your fork:{" "}
        <code>
          git clone https://github.com/&lt;your-username&gt;/shoal-station.git
        </code>
        , then enter the cloned folder.
      </li>
      <li>
        Install the <a href="https://cli.github.com/">GitHub CLI ↗</a>, and
        confirm <code>gh auth status</code> is usable as the Reviewer Node
        owner.
      </li>
      <li>
        Install the official extension:{" "}
        <code>gh extension install taco3064/gh-shoal</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        With a clean checkout, run <code>gh shoal init</code>. Verify the
        managed Issue Form and Summary Workflow match the canonical station, the
        canonical <code>.github/workflows/reviewer-summary.yml</code> is active,
        and Issues are enabled. Init repairs only that canonical workflow’s
        state when needed and enables Issues when disabled. It cannot perform
        the fresh-fork Actions UI step, change repository-level Actions policy,
        or enable unrelated workflows.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>
          Personally edit <code>README.md</code>
        </strong>{" "}
        to define your Review Policy. Commit and push your policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        Confirm the fork remains eligible: Issues enabled, supported canonical
        Review Request form, and allowed Summary Workflow digest. Your Reviewer
        Node appears after a later complete Network Scan and Pages publication.
        Forking alone does not guarantee immediate inclusion.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h2>AI-assisted mechanical setup</h2>
    <p>
      First complete the direct fork and manual GitHub Actions page confirmation
      yourself. Then copy this prompt into a local coding agent. This setup
      agent is separate from the agent you later select for{" "}
      <code>gh shoal review --agent &lt;agent&gt;</code>.
    </p>
    <SetupPrompt client:load />
    <h2>Policy, evidence, and review</h2>
    <p>
      <code>README.md</code> is your customizable Review Policy.{" "}
      <code>.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/review-request.yml</code> and{" "}
      <code>.github/workflows/reviewer-summary.yml</code> are Shoal-managed
      station surfaces. The Summary Workflow is trust machinery: byte-level
      edits, including whitespace or comments, change its digest. A Summary from
      a workflow outside the allowed canonical digest set is rejected. Run{" "}
      <code>gh shoal init</code> to repair managed file drift; complete GitHub’s
      Actions page confirmation yourself for a fresh fork.
    </p>
    <p>
      Official Automated Review runs in your local <code>gh shoal</code>{" "}
      extension with an explicitly selected local AI agent: <code>claude</code>,{" "}
      <code>codex</code>, <code>gemini</code>, <code>opencode</code>,{" "}
      <code>cursor</code>, <code>grok</code>, <code>qwen</code>, or{" "}
      <code>kimi</code>. The extension owns GitHub mutations and Shoal Protocol
      handling; Shoal does not host or automatically choose your agent. Manual
      Review remains possible when its formal Review / Re-review result comments
      follow the recognized Protocol format. Invalid formal result comments are
      observable maintenance facts, never a reputation score.
    </p>
    <a class="button secondary" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}reviewers/`}>
      Explore the Reviewer Directory →
    </a>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
